# cocaine_study (bluko_mrs) BIDS dataset

Philips PAR/REC T1w and DWI data converted to BIDS with
[dti_bids_conversion](https://github.com/hugofluhr/dti_bids_conversion)
(`dcm2niix` + custom sidecar handling).

## Known data issues

### Missing DWI data: sub-084

sub-084 has a T1w scan but no DWI (`dwi/`) data in this dataset. This is
a **raw data problem at the source**, not a conversion failure:
`raw_data/084_bluko_mrs_wipq64wb.rec` is missing entirely (only the
`.par` header is present). The original conversion attempt reported:
`Total number of slices (2621) not divisible by slices per 3D volume
(60) [acquisition aborted]` -- consistent with an aborted DWI
acquisition at the scanner.

Action needed: re-acquire or re-export DWI data for this subject if it
is available, otherwise it should be excluded from DWI analyses.

(sub-073 had the same issue -- a truncated `.rec` -- but a complete
replacement file was located and re-converted on 2026-09-02. Its DWI
data is now complete.)

### T1w protocol variant: sub-040, 044, 046, 062, 066, 077, 098

These 7 subjects' T1w scans were acquired under PAR header protocol name
`WIP sT1W_3D_TFE`, not the standard `WIP T1_NFB` used for the rest of the
cohort (raw PAR/REC filenames are identical across both -- the difference
only shows up in the PAR header's own `Protocol name` field and the
resulting sidecar `ProtocolName`/rescale/orientation values). This is
flagged by `bids-validator` as `INCONSISTENT_PARAMETERS` (code 39).

Both are Philips 3D T1-weighted structural sequences with matching
TR/TE, but they are not the same acquisition, and the difference is not
visible from filenames alone. Confirm with the study team whether this
was a deliberate protocol change partway through data collection before
treating these subjects' T1w data as equivalent to the rest of the
cohort in analysis.

### `subject_lut.tsv`

`subject_lut.tsv` at the dataset root is provenance metadata (original
PAR filename, patient name, scan date, protocol, conversion timestamp)
written by the conversion pipeline -- not a BIDS data file. It is
excluded from validation via `.bidsignore`.
